  <section|Mathematical content and status><label|mathematical-content-and-status>

  The manuscript reorganizes the local proof of
  <verbatim|YM.RG08.Flat.toward> as two mathematical arguments: a neutral
  weighted-kernel convolution estimate and an exact quadratic representative
  identity. It states the finite-label weighted row/column and
  first-difference costs explicitly, including the powers <verbatim|L^{-2}>,
  <verbatim|L^2>, and <verbatim|L^{-3}>. The scalar bound used in centering
  is proved in the text. The product bound is obtained by the triangle
  inequality for cover expense, Tonelli/Fubini on nonnegative absolute
  majorants, and multiplication of the row/column constants. Its coefficient
  is <verbatim|m^2 q (2/tau)p/L>, where <verbatim|m> is the common finite
  face-label cardinality.

  The zero-sum replacement of the outgoing kernel by its centered difference
  is proved from neutrality. The separate neutrality and
  simultaneous-translation invariance conclusions use the source's travel and
  covariance assumptions; their proofs are given at the level of cover sums
  and changes of variables. The matrix identity is derived in the manuscript:
  it proves the mixed Schur identity by matrix multiplication from the two
  primal/dual input relations, and proves each inherited carrier identity
  from the floor equalities and diagonal tower identity.

  This write-up is newly reorganized prose; it is not a literal translation
  of Lean helper structure. The independent reviewer has been asked to check
  the cover-path estimate, label sums, and finite-period reindexing. No
  external literature theorem is invoked: the arguments are elementary
  weighted-sum and finite-dimensional matrix calculations, and the local
  source proof was directly inspected.

