  <section|Constants and normalization cross-check><label|constants-and-normalization-cross-check>

  For order two, the source Atlas bounds are row cost <verbatim|q/L^2>,
  column cost <verbatim|q L^4/L^2=qL^2>, and first-difference row cost
  <verbatim|p/L^3>. The manuscript keeps each fixed input/output type in
  these inequalities; each finite-type sum is counted once explicitly. The
  centered row coefficient per fixed output label is <verbatim|(2/tau)p/L^3>;
  summing over output labels gives <verbatim|m(2/tau)p/L^3>. The root column
  per fixed input label is <verbatim|qL^2>; summing over input labels gives
  <verbatim|mqL^2>. Their product is <verbatim|m^2q(2/tau)p/L>, which equals
  <verbatim|YM.RG08.Packets.neutralCoin> with both finite label sets equal to
  the face labels. The pullback matrix orientation is <verbatim|M^T A N>; in
  <verbatim|toward>, the root kernel is matched by the <verbatim|Y> carrier
  and the outgoing kernel by the <verbatim|H> carrier. The inherited
  identities consequently produce <verbatim|N_A> on the left of the fine
  representative and <verbatim|M_A> on its right, matching the orientation of
  <verbatim|YM.RG08.Flat.poised>.

  <section|Remaining construction obligations><label|remaining-construction-obligations>

  This local unit does not establish that the selected histories satisfy
  their order-two Atlas bounds, exact city covariance, matching, Floor
  conditions, or the travel condition. Those are hypotheses of
  <verbatim|toward> supplied by the construction. It also does not prove the
  separate scale funding, limiting kernel, higher-order observable, or Wilson
  bridge arguments recorded in the other unit audit. The manuscript's
  finite-label statement is the rank-one specialization used here; no claim
  is made for general rank.

  <section|Reads and commands actually performed><label|reads-and-commands-actually-performed>

  Targeted source reads:

  <\verbatim-code>
    sed -n '1,180p' Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Inherit.lean

    sed -n '1,110p' Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Projected.lean

    sed -n '1,130p' Lean/YM/RG08/Packets/Torus.lean

    sed -n '1,130p' Lean/YM/Lattice/Site.lean

    sed -n '1,130p' Lean/YM/Lattice/Subdivision.lean

    sed -n '1,70p' Lean/YM/CellFourier/Shuttle.lean

    sed -n '1,85p' Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Crossing.lean

    sed -n '1,180p' Lean/YM/RG08/Packets/FlatStep.lean

    sed -n '1,240p' Lean/YM/RG08/Packets/Lines.lean

    sed -n '1,220p' Lean/YM/RG08/Packets/Mixed.lean

    sed -n '1,190p' Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Atlas.lean

    sed -n '1,130p' Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Discrete.lean

    sed -n '1,120p' Lean/YM/RG08/Packets/Swing.lean

    sed -n '1,150p' Lean/YM/RG08/Packets/Pushed.lean

    sed -n '1,110p' Lean/YM/RG08/Packets/Norm.lean

    sed -n '1,70p' Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Stacks.lean

    sed -n '58,68p' Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/UseRows.lean

    sed -n '55,105p' Lean/YM/PREC/Stacks.lean

    sed -n '70,108p' Lean/YM/PREC/TreeMatch.lean

    rg -n 'inherited_precision\|def inherited\|theorem inherited'
    Lean/YM/PCalc Lean/YM/PREC Lean/YM/RG08 Lean/YM/Pert

    rg -n 'atlas_difference\|def centered\|def Folded\|def charge\|def
    expense\|def delta\|def neutral\|def city\|def
    travels\|pass_push\|invariant' Lean/YM/Pert Lean/YM/RG08/Packets

    rg -n 'expense_sep\|def sep\|delta_fine\|use_head2\|def pass'
    Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk Lean/YM/RG08/Packets

    rg -n 'theorem town_hall\|def Matches\|structure Inputs\|structure
    Diagonal\|structure Floor\|theorem pass_push\|def centered'
    Lean/YM/RG08/Packets Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk Lean/YM/PREC
  </verbatim-code>

  No Lean files were edited; no Lean build, LaTeX build, or blueprint checker
  was run. The article now states the fixed-label Atlas bounds, proves the
  centered path estimate at fixed output type, and derives both the
  finite-matrix product and transpose match by explicit quotient-fibre
  reindexing. Independent review is pending. <verbatim|git diff --check>
  passed after the revision.

